From e2667cb282f52887ddd40795b324982be42a63db Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: custom_ffmpeg <custom_ffmpeg@localhost>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 19:50:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] picture manager: do not read the parent PCS after posting it
 to RC

svt_aom_picture_manager_kernel_iter() posts a started picture to rate
control and only then walks entry_ppcs->released_pics to set
dec_order_of_last_ref on the references the picture retires. Once the
picture is posted it can be encoded and packetized, the application can
take the packet and send the next frame, and rate control can release the
parent PCS, which resource coordination and picture decision then reuse
for the new input. In low delay the PPCS pool holds a single entry, so
this happens as soon as the picture manager thread is descheduled between
the post and the loop.

The loop then reads the next picture's decode_order and released_pics:
the reference that should have been retired keeps dec_order_of_last_ref ==
UINT64_MAX and is never released, ref_buffer_available_semaphore is not
posted, and picture decision blocks in send_picture_out() for the next
reference picture while the application waits in
svt_av1_enc_get_packet(). Seen as intermittent 15 s watchdog failures of
OnTheFlyRejectTest.* (SvtAv1ApiTests, RTC low-delay CBR, flat_max_refs 1,
ref_pic_list_length 2) when the test runs on a loaded machine; state at
the hang: picture 7 waiting on the semaphore, ref_pic_list = {6 with
dec_order_of_last_ref 7, 5 with UINT64_MAX}.

Mark the released references and clear the input queue entry before the
post. Only the picture manager thread reads these fields, so the order
does not change the encode.

Not fixed upstream as of 2026-10 (master still reads entry_ppcs after the
post); same class as the snapshot fix in send_picture_out() of upstream
commit 87f50f6f ("Fix three tsan data race issues").
---
 Source/Lib/Codec/pic_manager_process.c | 28 +++++++++++++++++---------
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+), 10 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Lib/Codec/pic_manager_process.c b/Source/Lib/Codec/pic_manager_process.c
index 1f75b1e..658e718 100644
--- a/Source/Lib/Codec/pic_manager_process.c
+++ b/Source/Lib/Codec/pic_manager_process.c
@@ -874,16 +874,14 @@ EbErrorType svt_aom_picture_manager_kernel_iter(void* context) {
             // off in low layers.
             child_pcs->ppcs->refresh_frame_context = REFRESH_FRAME_CONTEXT_BACKWARD;
         }
-        EbObjectWrapper* out_results_wrapper;
-        // Get Empty Results Object
-        svt_get_empty_object(context_ptr->picture_manager_output_fifo_ptr, &out_results_wrapper);
-        RateControlTasks* rc_tasks = (RateControlTasks*)out_results_wrapper->object_ptr;
-        rc_tasks->pcs_wrapper      = child_pcs->c_pcs_wrapper_ptr;
-        rc_tasks->task_type        = RC_INPUT;
-
-        // Post the Full Results Object
-        svt_post_full_object(out_results_wrapper);
-        // Remove the Input Entry from the Input Queue
+        // Mark the references released by this picture and remove it from the
+        // input queue before posting it to rate control. Once posted, the
+        // picture can be encoded and packetized and its parent PCS released and
+        // reused for the next input picture (at once with the single-PPCS pool of
+        // low delay), so entry_ppcs must not be read after the post: a stale
+        // read marked the wrong reference, the released one stayed in
+        // ref_pic_list and picture decision blocked forever on
+        // ref_buffer_available_semaphore.
         input_entry->input_object_ptr = NULL;
         svt_block_on_mutex(enc_ctx->ref_pic_list_mutex);
         for (uint32_t i = 0; i < enc_ctx->ref_pic_list_length; i++) {
@@ -897,6 +895,16 @@ EbErrorType svt_aom_picture_manager_kernel_iter(void* context) {
             }
         }
         svt_release_mutex(enc_ctx->ref_pic_list_mutex);
+
+        EbObjectWrapper* out_results_wrapper;
+        // Get Empty Results Object
+        svt_get_empty_object(context_ptr->picture_manager_output_fifo_ptr, &out_results_wrapper);
+        RateControlTasks* rc_tasks = (RateControlTasks*)out_results_wrapper->object_ptr;
+        rc_tasks->pcs_wrapper      = child_pcs->c_pcs_wrapper_ptr;
+        rc_tasks->task_type        = RC_INPUT;
+
+        // Post the Full Results Object
+        svt_post_full_object(out_results_wrapper);
     }
 
     svt_block_on_mutex(enc_ctx->ref_pic_list_mutex);
